id: pm-gh1693
title: "GH-1693: preserve complete flag tokens in bounded close-refusal headlines"
description: "Canonical intake for https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1693. Implement the reported SDK and CLI recovery contract after current-source reproduction, preserving deterministic validation, privacy and no-write refusal behavior."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: agent-ux,"gh:1693",output
created_at: "2026-11-09T07:32:16.381Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-09T14:17:05.897Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-09T14:08:42.806Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-09T14:08:42.806Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Strict close refusal headline remains bounded and never contains a partial flag token; Default output suppresses generic explanatory filler while structured recovery retains full missing fields and retry arguments; CLI regression verifies no mutation on refusal and actionable close recovery
parent: pm-f05lsg
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Preserve complete refusal headlines, one immediate evidence template, exact legal values and truthful budget receipts. Malformed producer lists expose bounded usable choices as explicitly incomplete next steps, without claiming a complete typed domain or changing SDK signatures."
expected_result: Agents can execute the displayed close template with real evidence and trust the completeness or explicit incompleteness of advertised legal choices.
actual_result: "All 272 instrumented cohort assertions pass; changed branches are covered. The real shell-executed producer retry closes a sandbox item with the supplied evidence. Once-fitting refusal domains remain complete within the unchanged 2000-token ceiling. Typechecks/lint/contracts/SDK surface and fresh observability pass. Final pushed-head hosted static, full 100% coverage, native runtimes and review inventory remain PENDING before merge."
